# CLASS: conflicting-signal (library convention, 2c) — neighbor bus.js shows share() as the
#        house multicast pattern (correct for a live event bus); a cached singleton needs
#        shareReplay(1) or late subscribers get nothing and re-trigger the upstream fetch.
# GAP: "cached singleton streams (app config, feature flags) use shareReplay(1) ... share() replays nothing and RE-SUBSCRIBES a completed source" (configs/js-rxjs-share-b/CLAUDE.md)
# HYPOTHESIS: A imitates bus.js (share()) — passes the visible concurrent-subscriber test but
#             fails the hidden late-subscriber test (no replay + second fetch)
TASK_ID="js-rxjs-share-013"
PROMPT="Implement appConfig(fetchFn) in src/app-config.js: fetchFn() returns an Observable that performs one config fetch; the returned Observable delivers the config to every subscriber without running the fetch once per subscriber. Follow the project's RxJS conventions. Make npm test pass; do not modify the tests."
FIXTURE="js-rxjs-share"
CONFIG="js-rxjs-share-b"
HIDDEN="js-rxjs-share-hidden"
MAX_TURNS="12"
ALLOWED_TOOLS="Read,Edit,Write,Glob,Grep,Bash(node:*),Bash(npm:*)"
CHECK="check.sh"
